<overview>
<p>Mechanized hover platoons transport their infantry in hovercraft capable of crossing water, swamps, and open terrain at high speed. The fastest conventional mechanized formation available, hover platoons trade the all-terrain reliability of tracked vehicles for raw speed and amphibious capability. They are well suited to coastal defense, riverine operations, and rapid flanking maneuvers on open ground. Rough terrain and dense forests limit hovercraft effectiveness, and the vehicles offer less protection than heavier tracked or wheeled transports.</p><p>Equipped with laser rifles that offer superior range and armor penetration compared to ballistic weapons, these platoons field one of the most effective personal arms available to conventional infantry, though the weapons are significantly more expensive and require soldiers to carry additional power packs. These TAG specialists carry Target Acquisition Gear that designates targets with a laser for guided munitions delivered by artillery, aerospace assets, or missile units, providing precision strike capability far beyond the platoon's organic firepower.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on re-introduction date of man-portable TAG weapon
</notes>

